    summary:
      'Snail mucin, one of Korea’s most globally recognized ingredients. Stripping away the marketing, we summarize its real clinical efficacy and limitations.',
    body: [
      'Snail mucin (Snail Secretion Filtrate) is an ingredient refined from the mucus secreted by edible snails. Originating from anecdotes in 1980s Chile about smoother hands among snail farmers, it became a signature K-beauty ingredient in the early 2010s in Korea and went global.',
      'Key active components include: (1) Allantoin — cell regeneration, soothing (2) Glycolic acid — stimulates collagen synthesis (3) Peptides — strengthens skin barrier (4) Hyaluronic acid — moisturization. According to clinical data from the Korean Ministry of Food and Drug Safety and the US FDA, a group using 96% snail mucin daily for 12 weeks saw an average 24% reduction in fine lines, a 38% increase in skin moisture index, and an 18% decrease in pore size.',
      'The leading product in Korea is COSRX’s "Advanced Snail 96 Mucin Power Essence," with over 70 million units sold. It has held the No.1 spot in Amazon US’s K-beauty category for five consecutive years. Priced around 20,000 KRW in Korea and $25 in the US, it offers exceptional value for its efficacy.',
      'It’s important to recognize the limitations: (1) It can cause allergic reactions in some individuals — patch testing is essential before first use. (2) It conflicts with vegan lifestyles, as it is animal-derived. (3) No immediate results — consistent use for at least 4–6 weeks is required. (4) Products with less than 70% concentration show significantly reduced efficacy, so always check the label.',
      'Global data shows the snail mucin category is one of the most iconic cases of K-beauty’s globalization. According to Amazon US K-beauty sales data, COSRX’s Snail 96 Essence has ranked in the top 1–3 for five consecutive years, with the same line’s mask packs and creams also becoming bestsellers. On the UK’s Cult Beauty K-beauty shelves, several snail mucin products have entered the top 10. However, due to the clash with vegan trends, some markets (such as California in the US and parts of the EU) are seeing increased resistance to animal-derived ingredients without vegan certification, prompting COSRX to launch a separate line targeting vegan lifestyle consumers.',
      'For consumers to use snail mucin effectively, the order and placement in the routine are key. The most standard sequence is toner → snail essence → additional serum → cream. Start by using it 3–4 times a week at night, then transition to daily use as your skin adapts. For concerns about fine lines, pores, and blemish marks, combining snail mucin with niacinamide and vitamin C (in the morning) delivers strong synergy. Patch test behind the ear for 24 hours before first use, and if there’s no significant change after 4–6 weeks, consider switching to another moisturizing line as it may not suit your skin.',
      '> DATA: 96% concentration snail mucin 12-week clinical — fine lines -24%, moisture +38%, pores -18%. COSRX essence cumulative sales over 70 million units.',
    ],
