      'In the broader Y2K comeback, frosty lips are less a standalone trend and more a branch of the mega-trend of \'reinterpreted shine.\' Glossy body oils, metallic manicures (like previously covered glass nails), and pearl-infused eyeshadows are all growing in tandem. According to NPD Group\'s Q1 2026 report, US mass-market lip sales in the pearl/metallic category rose 47% year-on-year, while matte sales stagnated. In Japan, more restrained \'flicker pearl\' (micro-particle) lines are popular, while in Korea, the \'glow core\' technique—concentrating metallics on the inner lips—is emerging as a new trend.',
