      'Glass Nails is a minimalist glossy nail style started by Korean nail artists around 2022 that has spread globally. The key feature is a smooth, glass-like shine, with the main difference from regular glossy nails being the depth of reflection and the transparency of the color.',
      'The core technique involves a four-step process: (1) applying two layers of base coat for thickness, (2) adding one or two thin layers of color, (3) applying mirror or chrome powder with a gloss enhancer, and (4) finishing with a thick glass-effect top coat. It takes about 30% longer than a regular manicure but lasts an average of over 14 days.',
      'According to Pinterest data, searches for \'glass nails\' rose by 240% year-on-year from December 2025 to April 2026, and the #glassnails hashtag on TikTok surpassed 1.8 billion views. The most popular colors are light beige, pale pink, ice blue, and sage green, especially suited for spring and summer.',
